On 9/2/06, HeliodoR <exitconsole@gmail.com> wrote:
> > Well, {fe'ire'a} is 2 words in a cmavo cluster. So it's {fE'i rE'a}.
> > mu'o mi'e komfo,amonan
>
> But you can say them as one word, can't you?

If you mean to ask, can you stress them so that they become a lujvo,
then no. If you mean, can you stress E in re'a and have them be
interpreted the same (as two cmavo), then I think yes. I think there
might be a danger of confusion if you say them directly after a
brivla, and you don't stress the brivla.

